course: dictionary
lesson: 15901
title: Un- words and unloved
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The start of a word can change its meaning. The little word un- at the front often means not. «The old bench in the park was unloved and covered in weeds.» Un- means not, and loved means cared for, so unloved means not cared for. The weeds show that nobody has been looking after the bench.
explain: Read the words around it to be sure. «Mia felt unloved when nobody came to her birthday party.» The clue is nobody came: Mia was not loved or thought about that day, so she felt sad and alone. Swap in not loved, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Unloved can describe things as well as people and pets. «The puppy was unloved until a kind family took it home.» Before the family came, nobody cared for the puppy. Unloved things are often not wanted, used or looked after.
fact: Un- at the start of a word often means not.
fact: «Unloved» means not loved or cared for by anyone.
fact: Unloved can describe people, pets, toys, buildings or places.
fact: «Unloved» often shows sadness or loneliness in stories.
fact: Other un- words: «unhappy» means not happy; «unkind» means not kind.
exercise: «The old bench in the park was unloved and covered in weeds.» What does unloved mean? | Very loud and busy | Painted bright red by the council | *Not loved or cared for | Brand new and shiny
exercise: The little word un- at the start of a word often means what? | Happy | Very big | *Not | Again
exercise: «Mia felt unloved when nobody came to her party.» Which words give you the clue? | *nobody came to her party | her party was loud | Mia felt | when
test: Which word means the opposite of unloved? | Hidden | Lonely | Unused | *Loved
test: «The puppy was unloved until a kind family took it home.» Why was the puppy unloved before? | It could not bark | It was too big to be a puppy | *Nobody was caring for it | It had a new home
exam: «An unloved park needs care.» What does unloved mean here? | *Not cared for, so it needs looking after | Very bright and colourful | Very happy and full of people | Brand new and clean
